==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{der|ru|cu|студъ|t=cold}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*studenъ|gloss=cold}}, from {{m|sla-pro|*studъ|gloss=cold, shame}} and thus cognate with {{m|ru|стыд|t=shame}}. Compare {{cog|pl|ostuda}}, {{cog|bg|студ}}.

Vasmer links the PIE root with {{der|ru|ine-pro|*(s)tewd-}} which, that being true, would expand the list of cognates to the likes of {{cog|sa|तुदति|t=to vex, to bother}}, {{cog|sa|तोद|t=instigator, propeller}}, {{cog|la|tundō|t=to beat, to crush}}, {{cog|grc|Τῡδεύς|t=Tydeus}}, {{cog|de|stoßen}} and {{cog|en|stot}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|сту́жа}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|сту́жа}}

# [[severe]] [[cold]], [[hard]] [[frost]] {{C|ru|Temperature}}
